# `Work.MotK.LinkCertTGenInf` — the *affine* Crauder–Katz link certificate for the T-twist

This is audit node **T8 / `linkCert_TK`** (`MOTIVIC_C6_R4_LEAD.md` §3.2, the K-route deliverable
`LK_T` of `MOTIVIC_S45_LEAD.md` §6): for an arbitrary base field `K` (char `≠ 5`, infinite) and an
arbitrary Kummer class `h : K` (`h ≠ 0`), the twist fields of the Klein curve by `h` and by `h²`
are linked by an affine certificate in the sense of `Work.MotV.LinkCert`.

## What has to be produced (the route)

`LinkCert K F₁ F₂` asks for `F G : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K`, `F G ≠ 0`,
`Φ : Localization.Away F ≃ₐ[K] Localization.Away G`, a height-one point `zP` with `G ∈ zP.asIdeal`,
`resF K zP ≃ₐ[K] RatFunc F₁`, all other height-one primes containing `G` junk (`JunkClass`), and all
height-one primes containing `F` either of class `RatFunc F₂` or junk.

### The chart conventions (settled — see `TwAmb` notes below)

Both sides of the link are `ℙ³`s embedded in the Klein `ℙ⁴`:

* **source** `H_s = {v₀ = 0}` with affine chart `v₄ = 1`, coordinates `(v₁,v₂,v₃)`;
* **target** `H_t = {w₀ = 0}` with affine chart `w₄ = 1`, coordinates `(w₁,w₂,w₃)`;
* the map is `f = kleinTwP ∘ kleinTwStereo : H_s ⤏ H_t` (it lands in `H_t` by
  `KleinTwQ_stereo` + `q(p) = 0`), with inverse `π_p ∘ kleinTwR`, where `π_p` is the *linear*
  projection from `p` to `H_s`; on `H_t` the map `kleinTwR` lands in the quadric
  (`kleinTwQ_kleinTwR_of_zero`);
* `p` is a `K`-rational point of `{q = 0}` with `p₀ ≠ 0` — e.g. `p = (1, 0, 1, b/(a h), 0)`.

The two divisor equations are

* **source** `kleinTwFhom a b h p v = b(p,v) · kleinTwS (kleinTwStereo p v)`  (degree 11 in `v`):
  its dehomogenisation is the `LinkCert` field `G`, and `zP` is the prime of its `s∘y` factor;
* **target** `kleinTwGhomV a b h p w = b(p, kleinTwR w) · kleinTwSDualV w`  (degree 6 in `w`):
  its dehomogenisation is the `LinkCert` field `F`.

## State of the workspace (this stretch) — the obstruction of the previous session is RESOLVED

