## Dead ends verified (do not retry)

* The *naive* twisted target data (`kleinTwSDual`, i.e. the plain twist of `s'`) does **not** satisfy
  I2'/I3'/I4' — use `kleinTwSDualV` (`TwDataMod5`).  The correction is exactly the mod-`5` weight
  bookkeeping recorded above; no CAS counterexample survives.
* `F = G` with `Φ = id`: impossible.  It would need `JunkClass K zP`, i.e. `F₀` with
  `GeomRuled K F₀` and `RatFunc F₀ ≅ RatFunc F₁`; with `ConstantsOnly K F₁` (`CR5`/`T5`) and the
  proved cancellation `algEquiv_ratFunc_cancel` (`C4`) this forces `F₀ ≅ F₁` and hence
  `¬ GeomRuled K F₀`.  Moreover `GeomRuled K F₁` is false for a genus-one function field (a
  non-constant rational map `ℙ¹ → C`, `g(C) ≥ 1`, contradicts Hurwitz).
* `F ∈ K^*`: then `G` would be a unit too, contradicting `G ∈ zP.asIdeal`.
* Any `Φ` induced by a `K`-automorphism of `K[x₀,x₁,x₂]` moves `zP` to a prime of the same
  (non-junk) class `F₁` and would violate `F_all`.  A genuine Cremona transformation is required.
* For the inverse map: `π_p` is the linear projection from `p` to `H_s`; a "stereographic inverse"
  of the form `x - (q(x)/b(p,x))p` gives the same unit condition only up to a power of `b(p,Rw)`
  and is *not* the map used (both agree on `H_t` because `kleinTwR (H_t) ⊆ {q = 0}`).

